*
!node_modules
!packages/services/identity/node_modules
!packages/services/identity/dist
!packages/services/identity/prod.package.json
# Shared @kitchensink/identity-utils: the root node_modules symlink resolves to this path, so its
# built dist + dist-pointing manifest must be in the image or `node dist/main.js` crash-loops on the
# bare specifier (the @kitchensink/tracing failure class). The committed package.json exports ./src
# for fresh consumers; the image copies prod.package.json (which exports ./dist) over it instead.
!packages/utils/identity/dist
!packages/utils/identity/prod.package.json
# Shared @kitchensink/identity-db (S-I7) and @kitchensink/identity-core: same pattern as identity-utils
# above — both resolve via the root node_modules symlink, so their built dist + dist-pointing prod
# manifest must be in the image or the bare-specifier import crash-loops at boot. identity-core is also
# consumed by the recipe-service image below.
!packages/shared/identity-db/dist
!packages/shared/identity-db/prod.package.json
!packages/shared/identity-core/dist
!packages/shared/identity-core/prod.package.json
# Food service image (mirrors the identity allowlist): the service dist + prod manifest, plus the two
# shared @kitchensink runtime deps (clerk-verify, usda-client) whose root node_modules symlinks resolve
# to these dist + dist-pointing prod.package.json paths.
!packages/services/food-service/node_modules
!packages/services/food-service/dist
!packages/services/food-service/prod.package.json
!packages/shared/clerk-verify/dist
!packages/shared/clerk-verify/prod.package.json
# The shared Nest error-envelope mechanism, imported by all three services' ApiExceptionFilter.
!packages/shared/nest-error-envelope/dist
!packages/shared/nest-error-envelope/prod.package.json
!packages/shared/messaging/dist
!packages/shared/messaging/prod.package.json
!packages/clients/usda/dist
!packages/clients/usda/prod.package.json
# Recipe service image (feature 001; mirrors the food allowlist): the service dist + prod manifest, plus
# the three shared @kitchensink runtime deps (recipe-core, food-service-client, clerk-verify) whose root
# node_modules symlinks resolve to these dist + dist-pointing prod.package.json paths. (identity-core,
# also a recipe-service runtime dep, is already allowlisted above alongside identity-db.)
!packages/services/recipe-service/node_modules
!packages/services/recipe-service/dist
!packages/services/recipe-service/prod.package.json
!packages/shared/recipe-core/dist
!packages/shared/recipe-core/prod.package.json
!packages/clients/food-service/dist
!packages/clients/food-service/prod.package.json
!packages/clients/recipe-service/dist
!packages/clients/recipe-service/prod.package.json
# The GENERATED wire-contract leaf packages (CODING_STANDARDS §15.2). Each service's `main.ts` imports its
# schema package's published `CONTRACT_HASH` to run the drift-layer-3 skew assertion as the FIRST thing the
# process does, so these are runtime imports on the very first line of the boot path: without the dist and a
# dist-pointing prod manifest in the image, the container crash-loops before it can report why.
!packages/schemas/food/dist
!packages/schemas/food/prod.package.json
!packages/schemas/identity/dist
!packages/schemas/identity/prod.package.json
!packages/schemas/recipe/dist
!packages/schemas/recipe/prod.package.json
